00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:04.320
We want to make sure that we have our things saved

68
00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:07.880
differently, we're going to call this new enter key

69
00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:08.880
and hit save.

70
00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.520
Then close out of this.

71
00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.200
Yep, we want to use our user defined keyboard.

72
00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.320
We're going to select that new enter key mapping

73
00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:24.840
that we just made and hit open, then hit okay.

74
00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:26.000
It's thinking about it.

75
00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:30.600
Now we're going to close out of here.

76
00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.360
And it's going to say again, hey, you changed some stuff.

77
00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.000
Do you want to save this current definition?

78
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.680
And of course we did that on purpose.

79
00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:42.880
So we're going to click yes.

80
00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.120
It's going to close out.

81
00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.440
Now let's relaunch it and make sure our change is stuck.

82
00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:52.200
So I'm going to enter in my TSO user ID again

83
00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:54.500
and hit return.

84
00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.160
Hey, look at that.

